== 1. entropy of the Chapter 7 distributions (bits) ==
  v uniform 0..255     H= 8.000  max= 8.000  2^H=  256.0  KL to uniform=0.0000
  v dist := {1,1,2}    H= 7.929  max= 8.000  2^H=  243.7  KL to uniform=0.0708
  v dist :/ {1,1,2}    H= 7.596  max= 8.000  2^H=  193.5  KL to uniform=0.4039
  kind 6:3:1           H= 1.295  max= 1.585  2^H=    2.5  KL to uniform=0.2895
  kind uniform 0..2    H= 1.585  max= 1.585  2^H=    3.0  KL to uniform=0.0000

== 2. KL divergence is the G-test: G = 2 n KL (nats) ~ chi2 ==
  counts [6076, 2940, 984]: KL=0.000175 bits, G=2.424 p=0.298; Pearson X2=2.419 p=0.298

== 3. plug-in entropy is biased low on small samples ==
  n=  100 plug-in 6.253  Miller-Madow 6.833  true 7.929
  n=  300 plug-in 7.234  Miller-Madow 7.644  true 7.929
  n= 1000 plug-in 7.732  Miller-Madow 7.908  true 7.929
  n= 3000 plug-in 7.866  Miller-Madow 7.927  true 7.929
  n=10000 plug-in 7.911  Miller-Madow 7.929  true 7.929

